The number of moves is irrelevant, as is whether or not he was
alone/the game "just move[s] along".  There are actually two bugs in
one, here.  1) While the player was unconcious, he was able to tell
what exploded, and 2) he was blinded, even though he presumably had his
eyes shut.  What should have happened:

You faint from lack of food.  It explodes!  You regain consciousness!

Incidentally, this raises the question: currently, the game tells you
what you would see if you were awake while you're sleeping ("You fall
asleep.  The lichen touches you!"), even though you can't see it, and
shouldn't really know what's going on anyhow.  Of course, taking it to
the other extreme--"You fall asleep!  You die!  DYWYPI?"--doesn't make
sense, either.  I'd suggest that sleep ought to be treated more like
blindness--"You fall asleep!  It hits!"--so you have some idea of
what's going on, and do just appear to die from passing out.  Thoughts?

